<title>USA: May allocates $43 mln for profit sharing.</title>
<headline>May allocates $43 mln for profit sharing.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>May Department Stores Co said on Tuesday it allocated $43.3 million towards its employee profit sharing plan.</p>
<p>The allocation is a matching rate of 103 percent of employees' $42 million in matchable contributions for 1996, the largest such match in the retailer's history.</p>
<p>May said employees contributed a total of $66 million to the plan in 1996. The matching rate is determined by the earnings performance of the company and the price of May stock.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
